---
// ar-va.com: who I am and how I work (2026-11-28, user: the main domain is the landing page; brand.ar-va.com stays the
// reference). Written as Artur, in the first person, about the kind of work in any field; the products are the proof,
// kept short (user, 2026-11-28). Positioning: .agents/product-marketing.md. The blog's list returns here when the blog
// is public again (shared/site.ts).
import Layout from '@shared/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Writing from '../components/Writing.astro';
import { MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC } from '@shared/site';

const built = [
  { name: 'music.ar-va.com', href: 'https://music.ar-va.com', status: '', text: 'A Discogs collection shown as a shelf of covers, every album ready to play.' },
  { name: 'vincent.ar-va.com', href: 'https://vincent.ar-va.com', status: '', text: 'A light and dark Nextcloud theme built from the colours you choose.' },
  { name: 'anon.ar-va.com', href: 'https://anon.ar-va.com', status: '', text: 'A box for writing to me without giving your name.' },
  { name: 'Solaris', href: '', status: 'In progress', text: 'One system for a tattoo studio’s artists, manager and front desk.' },
];

const link = 'text-kikyo-600 dark:text-kikyo-400 underline underline-offset-3 hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-white';
const body = 'text-lg text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-pretty';
const h2 = 'font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white';
---
<Layout title="ARVA: digital craft, evermore" description="I’m Artur. I build web tools for the work that still happens in spreadsheets, group chats and software made for somebody else, and each one is made to stay useful for years.">
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 w-full pt-12 pb-24">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="font-bold text-5xl sm:text-6xl leading-[1.05] text-zinc-900 dark:text-white text-balance">Digital craft, evermore</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-pretty">
        I’m Artur. I build web tools for the work that still happens in spreadsheets, group chats and software made for
        somebody else. Each one is made to stay useful for years.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how" class={h2}>How I work</h2>
      <div class={`mt-4 space-y-4 ${body}`}>
        <p>
          Every trade has jobs that people still do by hand, or force a general-purpose tool to do, because nobody built
          for them. Those are the jobs I look for. I start with the person who does that work every day. Then I keep
          simplifying until they can use the tool on their first try.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of the effort goes into the parts nobody sees, so the part people use can stay plain. On music.ar-va.com a
          record turns at a true 33⅓ rpm, and Vincent’s tests run about a thousand generated themes through every
          contrast check.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where software could make a choice for the people using it, I leave the choice with them. Vincent hands over
          settings you apply yourself, and anon publishes a message only when its writer asks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="built">
      <h2 id="built" class={h2}>Built so far</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-zinc-200 dark:divide-zinc-800 border-y border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
        {built.map((b) => (
          <li class="py-4 grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6 sm:items-baseline">
            <span class="flex items-baseline gap-2 font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">
              {b.href ? <a class={link} href={b.href}>{b.name}</a> : b.name}
              {b.status && <span class="rounded-md bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">{b.status}</span>}
            </span>
            <span class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-pretty">{b.text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="leaf">
      <h2 id="leaf" class={h2}>The leaf</h2>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        My sign is the leaf of the <i>kashiwa</i> oak, which keeps its dry leaves all winter and drops them only when new
        ones open. The “evermore” in my slogan comes from that habit. <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/story">How the leaf is drawn</a> and <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/">the rules my work follows</a> are on brand.ar-va.com.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="yours">
      <h2 id="yours" class={h2}>In your field</h2>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        If your work has a job like this, handled in a spreadsheet or a chat thread because nothing fits it, I can build
        the tool for it. I take on projects for other people and do every part of the work myself, so you talk directly
        to the person writing the code.
      </p>
      <a class="btn-primary mt-6" href="mailto:contact@ar-va.com">Tell me about the job</a>
    </section>

    {MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC && <div class="mt-20"><Writing /></div>}
  </main>
</Layout>
